index 4479b53..d50f217 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,42 @@
 
 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
 
+## Phone verification during sign-up
+
+Sign-up collects account details and an international phone number, sends a six-digit
+SMS code, then verifies the code on the server before calling the existing account
+registration service. Passwords remain in component memory until that final request;
+they are not saved in sessions. Phone numbers are used to verify possession during
+this flow; the existing registration service still receives its username/password
+payload and does not persist the verified number.
+
+Configure `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`, `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`, and `TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER` in the
+server runtime environment (see `.env.example`). The sender must be an SMS-enabled
+Twilio number authorized for the destination. Missing credentials cause a visible
+service-unavailable error; no demo code or verification bypass is provided.
+Delivery uses the [Twilio Messages API](https://www.twilio.com/docs/messaging/api/message-resource).
+
+Serve the site over HTTPS. SMS messages end with `@<request-hostname> #<code>` so
+WebOTP and system autofill can bind the code to the current site. WebOTP is optional;
+manual entry, paste, and `autocomplete="one-time-code"` remain available. The listener
+starts before delivery and is aborted on manual submission, resend, editing details,
+and unmount.
+
+Challenges are stored in Astro's server-side session with a salted code digest,
+a five-minute expiry, and five verification attempts. Each session can request five
+messages per hour with a one-minute cooldown. Codes are consumed before registration;
+after an upstream registration failure, request a new code. Requests must have a
+matching Origin header because this project disables Astro's global origin check.
+The Node adapter provides the default filesystem session driver; deployments with
+multiple instances need a shared session driver and a shared, atomic rate limiter
+covering destination numbers and client IPs to prevent session-reset SMS abuse.
+The external registration service remains outside this repository; its direct API
+does not gain a verification requirement from this change.
+
+Run `node --test tests/phone-verification.test.ts` for the isolated SMS helper checks
+and `pnpm run build` for the production build. These commands do not start a server
+or send real SMS messages.
+
 
 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
